  "id": "12649d7b-440d-5064-aca7-1fdc3263ac68",
  "slug": "red-robin-style-whiskey-sauced-burger-with-onion-straws",
  "name": "Copycat Red Robin Whiskey River BBQ Burger with Onion Straws",
  "recipe_type": "main",
  "brief_description": "Homemade copycat Whiskey River burgers from Red Robin on your grill with all the fixings - tomato, lettuce, and yes, crispy onion straws.",
  "cuisine": null,
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "Combine onions and buttermilk in a bowl and soak at room temperature for 1 hour."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "Pour oil to a depth of 1 1/2 inches into a deep, heavy-bottomed skillet or pot or a deep-fat fryer; heat to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C)."
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "text": "Meanwhile whisk together flour, 1/4 teaspoon salt, black pepper, cayenne, and 1/4 teaspoon paprika in a large bowl for the breading. Remove onions from buttermilk, allowing excess to drip off. Toss onions in the breading until well coated."
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "text": "Set a wire rack on a rimmed baking sheet. Working in 3 batches, fry onions, turning occasionally to break up any clumps, until crisp and golden, 1 to 2 minutes. Transfer to wire rack to drain. Repeat with remaining onions."
    },
    {
      "position": 5,
      "text": "For rub, stir together 1/2 teaspoon smoked paprika, celery salt, chili powder, garlic powder, onion powder, and remaining 1/2 teaspoon salt in a small bowl. Shape beef into 4 patties, about 4 inches in diameter. Brush patties with oil; sprinkle both sides with rub."
    },
    {
      "position": 6,
      "text": "Preheat grill to medium-high and lightly oil grate. Grill patties, uncovered, about 5 minutes or until slightly charred."
    },
    {
      "position": 7,
      "text": "Flip patties; brush barbecue sauce evenly over patties. Continue cooking about 3 minutes more or until charred and a thermometer inserted into centers registers 160 degrees F (70 degrees C). Top patties with cheese; grill, covered, until cheese is melted, about 1 minute more. Grill buns, cut sides down, uncovered, until toasted, 30 seconds to 1 minute."
    },
    {
      "position": 8,
      "text": "Spread buns with mayonnaise and additional barbecue sauce. Fill buns with patties, onion straws, tomato, and lettuce. Serve immediately."
    }
  ],
  "servings": 4,
  "cooking_time_minutes": 15,
  "preparation_time_minutes": 35,
